  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Aid for communities in the Diocese of Chosica, Peru</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2016 the effects of climate change have been causing severe mudslides, frost and drought that severely affect crops used for animal feed. The rains and frosts also affect the health of children, the elderly and their livestock. The State has been developing programmes to adapt to climate change, but these are held in communities of more than 50 families whilst encouraging smaller communities to group together, something that is not possible due to distances and customs.
The project will target 400 Households (3595 individuals), living at high altitude (4,700m) with priority given to children and the elderly, in 12 communities spread across 12 remote rural districts in the department of Lima, with a focus on the following key areas: health (medication), clothing and advocacy.</narrative>
  </description>
